       * horizontal (per-row) IIR forward + backward
       * vertical   (per-column) IIR forward + backward
   - Instead of storing full 2D intermediate arrays y1 and y2,
     we use per-line (1D) temporary buffers for the forward pass
     and combine on the fly in the backward pass. This reduces
     memory traffic and improves cache behavior.
   - Horizontal rows and vertical columns are processed in parallel
     with OpenMP when enabled (each row/column is independent).
   - Coefficients involving exponentials are precomputed once.
*/
static
void kernel_deriche[[gnu::flatten, gnu::noinline]](int w, int h, DATA_TYPE alpha,
       DATA_TYPE POLYBENCH_2D(imgIn, W, H, w, h),
       DATA_TYPE POLYBENCH_2D(imgOut, W, H, w, h),
       DATA_TYPE POLYBENCH_2D(y1, W, H, w, h),
       DATA_TYPE POLYBENCH_2D(y2, W, H, w, h)) {
